WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.856 --> 00:00:15.556
worry, Ivy!"

2
00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:16.716
Penelope said.

3
00:00:16.736 --> 00:00:20.037
"That spider is only a daddy longlegs."

4
00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:24.238
She brushed the spider off the shower wall.

5
00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:26.859
"Just a part of beautiful nature!"

6
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.169
"I think nature is unnatural," Ivy said.

7
00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:35.030
Penelope laughed.

8
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.471
"You're funny, Ivy!"

9
00:00:39.011 --> 00:00:40.892
They continued toward the girls' cabins.

10
00:00:41.472 --> 00:00:44.534
At Cabin 6, Penelope threw open the screen door.

11
00:00:44.554 --> 00:00:46.154
"Here's our cabin!"

12
00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:50.776
Inside were bunk beds and shelves for personal items.

13
00:00:51.977 --> 00:00:54.858
Two girls were sitting on one bed, giggling together.

14
00:00:54.878 --> 00:01:01.893
"Ivy, say hi to your bunkmates—Clara and Willow," Penelope said.

15
00:01:01.913 --> 00:01:04.015
"That's my bunk.

16
00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:05.876
You can have this one."

17
00:01:07.257 --> 00:01:08.538
Ivy put her suitcase down.

18
00:01:08.558 --> 00:01:14.122
"Hello." "You girls make Ivy feel at home.

19
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:19.085
When the bugle sounds, come to the square for some Evergreen spirit!"

20
00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.086
Penelope said.

21
00:01:20.106 --> 00:01:24.369
"Why does she keep talking about Evergreen spirit?"

22
00:01:24.949 --> 00:01:25.489
Ivy thought.

23
00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.192
After the counselor left, the two girls looked at Ivy.

24
00:01:30.876 --> 00:01:33.018
"So what kind of music do you like?"

25
00:01:33.418 --> 00:01:34.158
Clara asked.

26
00:01:34.578 --> 00:01:36.440
"Yeah, do you like K-pop?"

27
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.580
Willow asked.

28
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.262
"Those singers are the cutest!"

29
00:01:41.442 --> 00:01:42.483
Ivy sat on her bunk.

30
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:44.184
It sagged in the middle.

31
00:01:44.684 --> 00:01:46.345
The springs made a loud squeak.

32
00:01:46.365 --> 00:01:50.548
"My favorite band is Graveyard Puppies."

33
00:01:51.848 --> 00:01:54.490
She opened her suitcase and pulled out the band's poster.

34
00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.932
Clara and Willow stared at the creepy image.

35
00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:02.749
Then Clara laughed nervously.

36
00:02:02.769 --> 00:02:05.111
"We'll have to check them out."

37
00:02:06.372 --> 00:02:08.114
A second later a bugle sounded.

38
00:02:09.475 --> 00:02:10.536
Willow looked relieved.

39
00:02:11.977 --> 00:02:13.838
"Time for the welcome games!"

40
00:02:13.858 --> 00:02:17.401
"See you at the square," Clara said.

41
00:02:20.203 --> 00:02:23.005
Ivy sighed and grabbed her sketch pad and colored pencils.

42
00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:26.228
She trudged behind the other campers walking to the square.

43
00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.762
Penelope stood in front with a male counselor.

44
00:02:31.782 --> 00:02:33.843
"Hello, campers!

45
00:02:34.423 --> 00:02:35.864
Let's play a get-acquainted game.

46
00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:37.625
Larry will explain the rules."

47
00:02:38.706 --> 00:02:41.248
Larry wore sunglasses and had long hair.

48
00:02:41.268 --> 00:02:43.990
"Yeah, so, you're going to say your name.

49
00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.132
And then say some animal that starts with the same initial.

50
00:02:48.913 --> 00:02:52.515
Like, hey, my name is Larry, and I love lizards."

51
00:02:53.716 --> 00:02:55.257
Ivy moved to the back of the group.

52
00:02:55.277 --> 00:03:01.574
"Like, this is the lamest," she whispered, opening her sketch pad.

53
00:03:02.635 --> 00:03:06.058
Clara picked a cheetah for her animal, and Willow chose a whale.

54
00:03:07.059 --> 00:03:09.181
Then Larry called on a boy named Ezra.

55
00:03:12.784 --> 00:03:14.906
know him from school," Ivy thought.

56
00:03:17.007 --> 00:03:18.308
Ezra froze for a second.

57
00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:22.552
"Uh, m-my name is Ezra," he said.

58
00:03:22.572 --> 00:03:26.636
"And I love er, elephants!"

59
00:03:29.316 --> 00:03:32.038
For the next few minutes, Ivy was busy drawing.

60
00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:35.079
Suddenly she noticed how quiet it was.

61
00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.241
She looked up to see everyone staring at her.

62
00:03:38.261 --> 00:03:40.802
"Your turn!"

63
00:03:41.082 --> 00:03:41.943
Penelope called.

64
00:03:43.064 --> 00:03:44.945
Ivy sighed and flipped through her sketches.

65
00:03:44.965 --> 00:03:52.369
"My name is Ivy, and I love ivy—poison ivy."

66
00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:56.091
She held up a drawing of the plant with three leaves.

67
00:03:56.111 --> 00:03:59.749
"Ew!" a few kids said.

68
00:04:00.749 --> 00:04:02.350
Ezra started scratching himself.

69
00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.012
"I got a rash from poison ivy last summer!"

70
00:04:07.193 --> 00:04:08.013
Willow frowned.

71
00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:11.095
"Poison ivy isn't an animal."

72
00:04:12.275 --> 00:04:12.956
Ivy shrugged.

73
00:04:12.976 --> 00:04:14.737
"I'm an independent thinker."

74
00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.202
Wes Wheezer, the bugle boy, blew his instrument again.

75
00:04:25.242 --> 00:04:26.263
It was time for dinner.

76
00:04:27.003 --> 00:04:30.105
As everyone headed to the mess hall, Ezra walked beside Ivy.

77
00:04:31.026 --> 00:04:32.828
Clara and Willow walked with them too.

78
00:04:32.848 --> 00:04:35.410
"Can I see more of your art?"

79
00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:36.551
Ezra asked.

80
00:04:36.571 --> 00:04:41.495
"You seem to have a lot of talent," Clara said politely.

81
00:04:42.716 --> 00:04:43.897
Ivy flipped through the pages.

82
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:46.479
"I was working on this self-portrait."

83
00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.441
She showed them her latest sketch.

84
00:04:50.402 --> 00:04:52.724
It was a drawing of Ivy looking terrified.

85
00:04:53.504 --> 00:04:54.906
Her mouth was wide open.

86
00:04:55.746 --> 00:05:00.044
In the background was Camp Evergreen with a scary, orange-and-yellow sky.

87
00:05:00.064 --> 00:05:04.090
"I call it 'The Scream,'" Ivy said proudly.

88
00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.375
"Because that's what this camp makes me feel like doing!"
